<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) PIN1 efflux carrier canalization on a Lockhart (1965)-growing hexagonal leaf blade with Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment: sequential 1°→4° vein-order emergence, open trees vs closed areoles vs decelerating no-branching (Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina and procambial venation network))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-6> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina and procambial venation network)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D viscoelastic cell-wall FEM, turgor-driven anisotropic cell expansion, or stress feedback on PIN1 polarity",
        "does_not_claim: Quantitative agreement of the simulated areole count (beta_1 = 4 on a 407-cell blade) with the specimen's 205 areoles; only the topological class (open tree vs reticulate) is compared",
        "does_not_claim: That Feugier et al. (2005) report closed loops under saturating Phi (withdrawn in Pass 3: the paper reports no branching under decelerating Phi, which the `decelerating_no_branching` regime reproduces)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 6-face hexagonal intracellular PIN1 pool conservation and face-competition algebra (`verify_hexagonal_pool_conservation_and_face_competition`): pool error 0.0, winner-take-all share 0.9978 (ref 0.9960), saturated bipolar share 0.5221 (ref 0.5180), 6-regime Pearson r = 0.9999",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated ridge + chromatic warmth segmentation of the cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton specimen (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 539x351 px): vein density 0.3585, Betti-1 = 205 closed areoles, mean compactness 0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Commitment-delay expressivity sweep tau_commit in {0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8} giving monotone non-increasing beta_1 (Spearman rho = -1.0)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Emergent growing-blade module (`simulate_growing_blade_canalization`): Feugier Eqs. 1-6 integrated on a 26x22 hexagonal mesh whose active blade mask expands by the Lockhart area law A(t) = A_0 exp(phi[(P-Y_0)t - kappa t^2/2]) (A(7)/A(2) = 2.399, arrest at 8 DAG) through four stages (2.0, 3.5, 5.0, 7.0 DAG) with marginal cell birth; 1°, 2°, 3°, 4° vein orders emerge sequentially (4 of 4 orders) with beta_1 = 0 at every stage in the accelerating open-tree regime, beta_1 = 4 closed areoles at 7 DAG under the Scarpella (2004) commitment lock, vein-cell fraction 0.86 (no discrete strands) under decelerating Phi, and no veins under k_1 = 0",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Templated topology scaffold (`simulate_hexagonal_venation_models`, Panels A-B): vein paths placed by a shortest-path template, ODEs relaxed on the scaffold, Betti-1 = 0 vs 16 graph readouts — relabelled in Pass 3 as a scaffold / Law 1 & Law 3 check, NOT an emergent result",
        "reported_in_source: Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236(4):366-375 hexagonal leaf lamina auxin S_i and directional PIN1 carrier P_ij ODEs with conserved total cellular carrier pool P_total = P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_ij; accelerating carrier-response functions Phi(J) produce branching vein patterns while linear or decelerating Phi produce no branching; conserved-pool competition yields higher auxin in veins than surrounding tissue",
        "reported_in_source: Lockhart (1965) J. Theor. Biol. 8:264-275: irreversible cell expansion rate (1/V)dV/dt = phi * max(0, P - Y) with wall extensibility phi, turgor P and yield threshold Y",
        "reported_in_source: Scarpella, Francis & Berleth (2004) Development 131:3445-3455: vein orders form sequentially (midvein, then secondaries, tertiaries, quaternaries) during blade expansion; preprocambial domains extend as freely ending strands and fuse with pre-existing veins; procambial identity, once acquired, is not lost",
        "reported_in_source: Scarpella, Marcos, Friml & Berleth (2006) Genes & Development 20:1015-1027 ProPIN1:PIN1-GFP imaging showing epidermal PIN1 convergence points and transient bipolar PIN1 cells bridging strands into closed areoles",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D hexagonal cellular lattice with Lockhart area growth and marginal cell addition mapped to a cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton; blade growth is applied to the area/mask only (no per-cell anisotropic expansion, no carrier dilution by growth)",
        "transfer_boundary: The 'closed areole' mechanism is Scarpella (2004/2006) procambial commitment, implemented as a sustained-flux lock, not a Feugier (2005) result" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Auxin flux vein / phyllotactic primordium in Arabidopsis thaliana" ;
