<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) PIN1 efflux carrier canalization on a Lockhart (1965)-growing hexagonal leaf blade with Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment: sequential 1°→4° vein-order emergence, open trees vs closed areoles vs decelerating no-branching — Code-to-model traceability: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-79) maps Laws 1-6 to Feugier Eqs. 1-6, Scarpella (2004/2006), Lockhart (1965) Eq. 1 and six named Lean 4 theorems with line-pinned loci; `simulate_growing_blade_canalization` and `simulate_hexagonal_venation_models` docstrings state what is emergent and what is templated; `morphoeval/math_kg_loops/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.yaml` registers 6 equations with lean_decl / lean_theorem / lean_locus / code_locus. Minor debit: Law 2's docstring text still describes the saturating case as \"Model B / Scarpella (2006)\" (L47-50) with the correction carried in the header rather than rewritten in place." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) PIN1 efflux carrier canalization on a Lockhart (1965)-growing hexagonal leaf blade with Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment: sequential 1°→4° vein-order emergence, open trees vs closed areoles vs decelerating no-branching — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The emergent growing-blade module (`simulate_growing_blade_canalization`, L862-1076) integrates the Feugier Eqs. 1-6 (flux kernel L933-1003, pool conservation error 0.0, flux antisymmetry error 0.0) on a Lockhart-growing mask (`lockhart_blade_area`, `blade_mask_at_growth_fraction`, L699-813) and reproduces Feugier's own dichotomy — accelerating Phi = J^2 → branching open tree (beta_1 = 0 at all four stages), decelerating Phi = J^2/(1+(J/K)^2) → no discrete branching (vein fraction 0.86) — plus the Scarpella (2004) commitment lock (L998-1001) that converts transient bipolar cells into closed areoles (beta_1 = 4). Debits: Panels A-B still render the Pass 2 shortest-path template (`simulate_hexagonal_venation_models`, L421-693) which is not an emergent result; the commitment lock is switched on by stage index (`commitment_on = ... s_idx >= 1`, L979) rather than by auxin history; the midvein is seeded by an apex convergence point (L948) rather than emerging; growth acts only on the mask (no per-cell expansion, no carrier dilution); emergent 3°/4° strands are 2-3 cells wide in the stage figure, wider than the single-file procambial strands of Scarpella (2006)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py L421–L693: Panels A-B topology comparison is a shortest-path template relaxed by the ODEs (now labelled as scaffold); still rendered in the main figure and still the source of 2 of the 15 measurements <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L421-L693>",
        "2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py L979–L979: Commitment lock gated by growth-stage index (s_idx >= 1) rather than by an auxin/flux history criterion <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L979-L979>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) PIN1 efflux carrier canalization on a Lockhart (1965)-growing hexagonal leaf blade with Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment: sequential 1°→4° vein-order emergence, open trees vs closed areoles vs decelerating no-branching — Morphometric validation: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1193-1400) returns 15 deterministic reference-anchored measurements: the 9 Pass 2 metrics (pool error 0.0, antisymmetry 0.0, dominant-face shares 0.9978/0.5221, Pearson r 0.9999, scaffold Betti-1 0/16, specimen Betti-1 205, compactness 0.7749) plus 6 new ones — Lockhart area fold change 2.399 (closed form 2.3989, Euler witness within 8.5e-5), sequential vein orders 4/4, open-tree final beta_1 = 0, committed final beta_1 = 4 (ref >= 1), decelerating vein-cell fraction 0.8575 (ref 1.0 +- 0.15), tau_commit Spearman rho = -1.0 — each with a k_1 = 0 negative control where applicable. Debits: 5 of the 6 new reference values come from the internally authored `growing_blade_reference.json`, the decelerating tolerance (+- 0.15) is loose, and the scaffold's dominant-face share, previously hard-coded, is now computed (L663-664) but still measured on a templated network." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py L1373–L1382: Decelerating no-branching metric anchored at ref 1.0 with +-0.15 tolerance — qualitative rather than quantitative reference <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L1373-L1382>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-allocation-regime-sweep-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-commitment-delay-betti1-spearman-rho>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-growing-blade-committed-reticulate-betti1-final>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-growing-blade-decelerating-vein-cell-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-growing-blade-open-tree-betti1-final>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-growing-blade-sequential-vein-orders-emerged>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-hexagonal-pin1-pool-conservation-error>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-lockhart-blade-area-fold-change-2-to-7-dag>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-model-a-open-tree-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-model-a-quadratic-dominant-face-share>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-model-b-closed-reticulate-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-model-b-saturating-dominant-face-share>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-pairwise-auxin-flux-antisymmetry-error>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-specimen-areole-compactness-mean>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-specimen-closed-areole-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
