<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier et al. (2005) Hexagonal Intracellular PIN1 Carrier Pool Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves exact state and rate conservation of total intracellular + membrane PIN1 efflux carriers across all 6 faces of each hexagonal leaf lamina cell, creating resource competition among faces for cytoplasmic PIN1 vesicles | Variables: P_{i,cyt}: cytoplasmic PIN1 carrier pool in cell i; P_{ij} (j=1..6): membrane PIN1 carrier density on face j of hexagonal cell i; P_{total}: conserved total cellular carrier pool; k_1, k_2: exocytosis and endocytosis rates; Φ(J_{i→j}): flux-dependent carrier recruitment function" ;
    dct:source "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236(4):366-375 Eqs. 4-6" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L160-L279>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L27-L56> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cytoplasmic_pin_pool (P_total P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 : Int) : Int :=
  P_total - (P1 + P2 + P3 + P4 + P5 + P6)
def membrane_face_rhs (k1 k2 Phi_j P_cyt P_j : Int) : Int :=
  k1 * Phi_j * P_cyt - k2 * P_j
theorem feugier_2005_hexagonal_pin_pool_conservation
    (P_total k1 k2 Phi1 Phi2 Phi3 Phi4 Phi5 Phi6 P_cyt P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 : Int) :
    cytoplasmic_pin_pool P_total P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 + (P1 + P2 + P3 + P4 + P5 + P6) = P_total ∧
    cytoplasmic_pool_rhs k1 k2 Phi1 Phi2 Phi3 Phi4 Phi5 Phi6 P_cyt P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 +
      (membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi1 P_cyt P1 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi2 P_cyt P2 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi3 P_cyt P3 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi4 P_cyt P4 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi5 P_cyt P5 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi6 P_cyt P6) = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_{i,cyt} + ∑_{j=1}^6 P_{ij} = P_{total},   dP_{i,cyt}/dt + ∑_{j=1}^6 dP_{ij}/dt = ∑_{j=1}^6 (k_2 P_{ij} - k_1 Φ(J_{i→j}) P_{i,cyt}) + ∑_{j=1}^6 (k_1 Φ(J_{i→j}) P_{i,cyt} - k_2 P_{ij}) = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.cytoplasmic_pin_pool" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.feugier_2005_hexagonal_pin_pool_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier et al. (2005) Winner-Take-All Open Tree vs Saturating Co-Polarized Face Law (Pass 3 note: the closed-loop attribution to Feugier is withdrawn; loop closure is Scarpella 2004/2006 commitment)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the two-face competition algebra: non-saturating superlinear exocytosis (Φ(J) = J^2) forces winner-take-all polarization onto a single efflux face per cell (open dendritic trees, β_1 = 0), whereas a saturated exocytosis ceiling lets two high-flux faces co-polarize (bipolar cells). Pass 3 correction: Feugier (2005) reports that decelerating/saturating Φ yields NO branching (the growing-blade `decelerating_no_branching` regime reproduces this, vein fraction -> ~0.9); the bipolar-cell loop closure in the leaf is attributed to Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment, formalised as Law 6. Code loci: templated scaffold #L421-L693, emergent growing-blade regimes #L862-L1076 | Variables: P_1, P_2: PIN1 carrier concentrations on two efflux faces of a hexagonal cell; P_{cyt}: shared cytoplasmic PIN1 pool; ΔS: downstream auxin concentration drop; Φ_{max}: saturated Hill exocytosis ceiling; β_1 = E - V + C: venation graph Betti-1 loop count" ;
    dct:source "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236(4):366-375 (PMID 15899502) Eqs. 7-11 & Figs. 3-7 (accelerating -> branching; decelerating -> no branching); Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev. 20:1015-1027 Figs. 3-5 (bipolar PIN1 cells)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L862-L1076>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L78-L98> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def model_a_quadratic_face_rhs (k1 k2 P_cyt dS P : Int) : Int :=
  k1 * (P * dS) * (P * dS) * P_cyt - k2 * P
def model_b_saturated_face_rhs (k1 k2 Phi_max P_cyt P : Int) : Int :=
  k1 * Phi_max * P_cyt - k2 * P
theorem feugier_2005_winner_take_all_vs_saturating_bipolar
    (k1 k2 Phi_max P_cyt dS P1 P2 : Int) :
    P2 * model_a_quadratic_face_rhs k1 k2 P_cyt dS P1 -
      P1 * model_a_quadratic_face_rhs k1 k2 P_cyt dS P2 =
      k1 * P_cyt * dS * dS * P1 * P2 * (P1 - P2) ∧
    P2 * model_b_saturated_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi_max P_cyt P1 -
      P1 * model_b_saturated_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi_max P_cyt P2 =
      k1 * Phi_max * P_cyt * (P2 - P1)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_2 dP_1/dt - P_1 dP_2/dt = k_1 P_{cyt} (ΔS)^2 P_1 P_2 (P_1 - P_2) (Model A, Φ(J)=J^2, open tree β_1=0)  vs  k_1 Φ_{max} P_{cyt} (P_2 - P_1) (Model B, Φ(J)=J^n/(K^n+J^n)→Φ_{max}, bipolar loop closure β_1>0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.model_a_quadratic_face_rhs" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.feugier_2005_winner_take_all_vs_saturating_bipolar" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier et al. (2005) Directional Carrier-Mediated Auxin Flux Antisymmetry Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves exact pairwise intercellular auxin flux conservation across every hexagonal cell-wall edge while demonstrating pure carrier-driven polar transport at homogeneous auxin concentration. Code loci: graph topology #L351-L419, growing-blade flux kernel #L933-L1003 | Variables: J_{i→j}: net intercellular auxin flux from hexagonal cell i to neighbor j; P_{ij}, P_{ji}: opposing plasma-membrane PIN1 carrier densities; S_i, S_j: intracellular auxin concentrations; D: passive apoplastic permeability" ;
    dct:source "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236(4):366-375 Eqs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L933-L1003>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L112-L124> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def carrier_auxin_flux (P_ij P_ji D S_i S_j : Int) : Int :=
  P_ij * S_i - P_ji * S_j + D * (S_i - S_j)
theorem feugier_2005_flux_antisymmetry_and_polarity (P_ij P_ji D S_i S_j S : Int) :
    carrier_auxin_flux P_ij P_ji D S_i S_j +
      carrier_auxin_flux P_ji P_ij D S_j S_i = 0 ∧
    carrier_auxin_flux P_ij P_ji D S S = (P_ij - P_ji) * S
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "J_{i→j} = P_{ij} S_i - P_{ji} S_j + D(S_i - S_j)  ⇒  J_{i→j} + J_{j→i} = 0  ∧  J_{i→j}(S,S) = (P_{ij} - P_{ji}) S" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.carrier_auxin_flux" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.feugier_2005_flux_antisymmetry_and_polarity" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lockhart (1965) Yield-Threshold Biomechanical Blade Growth Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Drives the growing hexagonal blade mesh on which the Feugier ODEs are integrated: blade area follows the Lockhart law (closed form A(7)/A(2) = 2.399, Euler check within 1e-3), new marginal cells are born as the allometric blade mask (half-width ∝ g^1.5, half-length ∝ g^0.5) expands, so vein orders emerge sequentially rather than from a prescribed template | Variables: A: blade area; φ: wall extensibility; P: turgor pressure; Y(t) = Y_0 + κ t: time-hardening wall yield threshold; κ: hardening rate; arrest at t* = (P − Y_0)/κ = 8 DAG with the script defaults (φ = 1.0, P = 0.6, Y_0 = 0.2, κ = 0.05)" ;
    dct:source "Lockhart (1965) J. Theor. Biol. 8(2):264-275 Eq. 1 (doi 10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9); Kuchen et al. (2012) Science 335(6072):1092-1096 (growth-field framing)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L699-L813>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L139-L163> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def lockhart_growth_rate (phi P Y : Int) : Int :=
  if Y < P then phi * (P - Y) else 0
theorem lockhart_1965_yield_threshold_growth (phi P P' Y : Int) (hphi : 0 < phi) :
    (P ≤ Y → lockhart_growth_rate phi P Y = 0) ∧
    (Y < P → 0 < lockhart_growth_rate phi P Y) ∧
    (P ≤ P' → lockhart_growth_rate phi P Y ≤ lockhart_growth_rate phi P' Y)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "(1/A) dA/dt = φ · max(0, P − Y(t)),   Y(t) = Y_0 + κ t   ⇒   A(t) = A_0 exp(φ[(P − Y_0) t − κ t²/2]) for t ≤ (P − Y_0)/κ, growth arrest thereafter" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.lockhart_growth_rate" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.lockhart_1965_yield_threshold_growth" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Vein-Graph Growth-Event Betti-1 Bookkeeping Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Classifies every canalization event during blade growth by its effect on the areole count: only fusion of a freely-ending strand with its own component (Scarpella et al. 2004) closes an areole, which is why the open-tree regime stays at β_1 = 0 across all four stages and the committed regime accumulates β_1 ≥ 1 after the lock activates | Variables: E: strand edges (vein-cell pairs joined by a PIN1 face with P ≥ P_vein); V: vein cells; C: connected components; β_1: closed areole count" ;
    dct:source "Scarpella, Francis & Berleth (2004) Development 131(14):3445-3455 (freely-ending domain fusion); Kang & Dengler (2004) Int. J. Plant Sci. 165(2):231-242 (vein-order hierarchy); standard graph cycle-rank identity" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L815-L860>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L180-L187> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def betti1 (E V C : Int) : Int := E - V + C
theorem vein_graph_growth_event_betti1 (E V C : Int) :
    betti1 (E + 1) (V + 1) C = betti1 E V C ∧
    betti1 E (V + 1) (C + 1) = betti1 E V C ∧
    betti1 (E + 1) V C = betti1 E V C + 1 ∧
    betti1 (E + 1) V (C - 1) = betti1 E V C
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "β_1 = E − V + C;  free-end extension (E+1,V+1,C): Δβ_1 = 0;  new seed (E,V+1,C+1): Δβ_1 = 0;  same-component fusion (E+1,V,C): Δβ_1 = +1;  cross-component fusion (E+1,V,C−1): Δβ_1 = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.betti1" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.vein_graph_growth_event_betti1" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Scarpella et al. (2004) Irreversible Procambial Commitment Lock Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Formalises the irreversible preprocambial → procambial transition that preserves transient bipolar PIN1 cells as permanent bridges, so closed areoles emerge in the committed regime; predicts and the script confirms a monotone non-increasing β_1(τ_commit) (Spearman ρ = −1.0 over τ ∈ {0.5,1,2,4,8}). Code loci: lock #L998-L1001, sweep #L1078-L1103 | Variables: P_ij: membrane PIN1 density on face j of cell i; P_commit: procambial commitment threshold; τ_commit: required sustained-flux duration; locked_ij: irreversible commitment flag (monotone non-decreasing in time)" ;
    dct:source "Scarpella, Francis & Berleth (2004) Development 131(14):3445-3455 (doi 10.1242/dev.01182); Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev. 20(8):1015-1027 (bipolar PIN1 cells)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L998-L1001>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L201-L217> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def commitment_lock (locked : Bool) (P P_commit : Int) : Int :=
  if locked then (if P < P_commit then P_commit else P) else P
theorem procambial_commitment_lock_monotone (P P_commit : Int) :
    P_commit ≤ commitment_lock true P P_commit ∧
    P ≤ commitment_lock true P P_commit ∧
    (P_commit ≤ P → commitment_lock true P P_commit = P) ∧
    commitment_lock false P P_commit = P
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "timer_ij ← (P_ij ≥ P_commit) ? timer_ij + dt : 0;   locked_ij ← locked_ij ∨ (timer_ij ≥ τ_commit);   P_ij ← locked_ij ? max(P_ij, P_commit) : P_ij" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.commitment_lock" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.procambial_commitment_lock_monotone" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier et al. (2005) Hexagonal Intracellular PIN1 Carrier Pool Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves exact state and rate conservation of total intracellular + membrane PIN1 efflux carriers across all 6 faces of each hexagonal leaf lamina cell, creating resource competition among faces for cytoplasmic PIN1 vesicles | Variables: P_{i,cyt}: cytoplasmic PIN1 carrier pool in cell i; P_{ij} (j=1..6): membrane PIN1 carrier density on face j of hexagonal cell i; P_{total}: conserved total cellular carrier pool; k_1, k_2: exocytosis and endocytosis rates; Φ(J_{i→j}): flux-dependent carrier recruitment function" ;
    dct:source "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236(4):366-375 Eqs. 4-6" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L160-L279>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L27-L56> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cytoplasmic_pin_pool (P_total P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 : Int) : Int :=
  P_total - (P1 + P2 + P3 + P4 + P5 + P6)
def membrane_face_rhs (k1 k2 Phi_j P_cyt P_j : Int) : Int :=
  k1 * Phi_j * P_cyt - k2 * P_j
theorem feugier_2005_hexagonal_pin_pool_conservation
    (P_total k1 k2 Phi1 Phi2 Phi3 Phi4 Phi5 Phi6 P_cyt P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 : Int) :
    cytoplasmic_pin_pool P_total P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 + (P1 + P2 + P3 + P4 + P5 + P6) = P_total ∧
    cytoplasmic_pool_rhs k1 k2 Phi1 Phi2 Phi3 Phi4 Phi5 Phi6 P_cyt P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 +
      (membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi1 P_cyt P1 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi2 P_cyt P2 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi3 P_cyt P3 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi4 P_cyt P4 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi5 P_cyt P5 +
       membrane_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi6 P_cyt P6) = 0
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_{i,cyt} + ∑_{j=1}^6 P_{ij} = P_{total},   dP_{i,cyt}/dt + ∑_{j=1}^6 dP_{ij}/dt = ∑_{j=1}^6 (k_2 P_{ij} - k_1 Φ(J_{i→j}) P_{i,cyt}) + ∑_{j=1}^6 (k_1 Φ(J_{i→j}) P_{i,cyt} - k_2 P_{ij}) = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.cytoplasmic_pin_pool" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.feugier_2005_hexagonal_pin_pool_conservation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier et al. (2005) Winner-Take-All Open Tree vs Saturating Co-Polarized Face Law (Pass 3 note: the closed-loop attribution to Feugier is withdrawn; loop closure is Scarpella 2004/2006 commitment)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the two-face competition algebra: non-saturating superlinear exocytosis (Φ(J) = J^2) forces winner-take-all polarization onto a single efflux face per cell (open dendritic trees, β_1 = 0), whereas a saturated exocytosis ceiling lets two high-flux faces co-polarize (bipolar cells). Pass 3 correction: Feugier (2005) reports that decelerating/saturating Φ yields NO branching (the growing-blade `decelerating_no_branching` regime reproduces this, vein fraction -> ~0.9); the bipolar-cell loop closure in the leaf is attributed to Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment, formalised as Law 6. Code loci: templated scaffold #L421-L693, emergent growing-blade regimes #L862-L1076 | Variables: P_1, P_2: PIN1 carrier concentrations on two efflux faces of a hexagonal cell; P_{cyt}: shared cytoplasmic PIN1 pool; ΔS: downstream auxin concentration drop; Φ_{max}: saturated Hill exocytosis ceiling; β_1 = E - V + C: venation graph Betti-1 loop count" ;
    dct:source "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236(4):366-375 (PMID 15899502) Eqs. 7-11 & Figs. 3-7 (accelerating -> branching; decelerating -> no branching); Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev. 20:1015-1027 Figs. 3-5 (bipolar PIN1 cells)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L862-L1076>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L78-L98> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def model_a_quadratic_face_rhs (k1 k2 P_cyt dS P : Int) : Int :=
  k1 * (P * dS) * (P * dS) * P_cyt - k2 * P
def model_b_saturated_face_rhs (k1 k2 Phi_max P_cyt P : Int) : Int :=
  k1 * Phi_max * P_cyt - k2 * P
theorem feugier_2005_winner_take_all_vs_saturating_bipolar
    (k1 k2 Phi_max P_cyt dS P1 P2 : Int) :
    P2 * model_a_quadratic_face_rhs k1 k2 P_cyt dS P1 -
      P1 * model_a_quadratic_face_rhs k1 k2 P_cyt dS P2 =
      k1 * P_cyt * dS * dS * P1 * P2 * (P1 - P2) ∧
    P2 * model_b_saturated_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi_max P_cyt P1 -
      P1 * model_b_saturated_face_rhs k1 k2 Phi_max P_cyt P2 =
      k1 * Phi_max * P_cyt * (P2 - P1)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_2 dP_1/dt - P_1 dP_2/dt = k_1 P_{cyt} (ΔS)^2 P_1 P_2 (P_1 - P_2) (Model A, Φ(J)=J^2, open tree β_1=0)  vs  k_1 Φ_{max} P_{cyt} (P_2 - P_1) (Model B, Φ(J)=J^n/(K^n+J^n)→Φ_{max}, bipolar loop closure β_1>0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.model_a_quadratic_face_rhs" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.feugier_2005_winner_take_all_vs_saturating_bipolar" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier et al. (2005) Directional Carrier-Mediated Auxin Flux Antisymmetry Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves exact pairwise intercellular auxin flux conservation across every hexagonal cell-wall edge while demonstrating pure carrier-driven polar transport at homogeneous auxin concentration. Code loci: graph topology #L351-L419, growing-blade flux kernel #L933-L1003 | Variables: J_{i→j}: net intercellular auxin flux from hexagonal cell i to neighbor j; P_{ij}, P_{ji}: opposing plasma-membrane PIN1 carrier densities; S_i, S_j: intracellular auxin concentrations; D: passive apoplastic permeability" ;
    dct:source "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236(4):366-375 Eqs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L933-L1003>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L112-L124> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def carrier_auxin_flux (P_ij P_ji D S_i S_j : Int) : Int :=
  P_ij * S_i - P_ji * S_j + D * (S_i - S_j)
theorem feugier_2005_flux_antisymmetry_and_polarity (P_ij P_ji D S_i S_j S : Int) :
    carrier_auxin_flux P_ij P_ji D S_i S_j +
      carrier_auxin_flux P_ji P_ij D S_j S_i = 0 ∧
    carrier_auxin_flux P_ij P_ji D S S = (P_ij - P_ji) * S
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "J_{i→j} = P_{ij} S_i - P_{ji} S_j + D(S_i - S_j)  ⇒  J_{i→j} + J_{j→i} = 0  ∧  J_{i→j}(S,S) = (P_{ij} - P_{ji}) S" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.carrier_auxin_flux" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.feugier_2005_flux_antisymmetry_and_polarity" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lockhart (1965) Yield-Threshold Biomechanical Blade Growth Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Drives the growing hexagonal blade mesh on which the Feugier ODEs are integrated: blade area follows the Lockhart law (closed form A(7)/A(2) = 2.399, Euler check within 1e-3), new marginal cells are born as the allometric blade mask (half-width ∝ g^1.5, half-length ∝ g^0.5) expands, so vein orders emerge sequentially rather than from a prescribed template | Variables: A: blade area; φ: wall extensibility; P: turgor pressure; Y(t) = Y_0 + κ t: time-hardening wall yield threshold; κ: hardening rate; arrest at t* = (P − Y_0)/κ = 8 DAG with the script defaults (φ = 1.0, P = 0.6, Y_0 = 0.2, κ = 0.05)" ;
    dct:source "Lockhart (1965) J. Theor. Biol. 8(2):264-275 Eq. 1 (doi 10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9); Kuchen et al. (2012) Science 335(6072):1092-1096 (growth-field framing)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L699-L813>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L139-L163> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def lockhart_growth_rate (phi P Y : Int) : Int :=
  if Y < P then phi * (P - Y) else 0
theorem lockhart_1965_yield_threshold_growth (phi P P' Y : Int) (hphi : 0 < phi) :
    (P ≤ Y → lockhart_growth_rate phi P Y = 0) ∧
    (Y < P → 0 < lockhart_growth_rate phi P Y) ∧
    (P ≤ P' → lockhart_growth_rate phi P Y ≤ lockhart_growth_rate phi P' Y)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "(1/A) dA/dt = φ · max(0, P − Y(t)),   Y(t) = Y_0 + κ t   ⇒   A(t) = A_0 exp(φ[(P − Y_0) t − κ t²/2]) for t ≤ (P − Y_0)/κ, growth arrest thereafter" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.lockhart_growth_rate" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.lockhart_1965_yield_threshold_growth" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Vein-Graph Growth-Event Betti-1 Bookkeeping Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Classifies every canalization event during blade growth by its effect on the areole count: only fusion of a freely-ending strand with its own component (Scarpella et al. 2004) closes an areole, which is why the open-tree regime stays at β_1 = 0 across all four stages and the committed regime accumulates β_1 ≥ 1 after the lock activates | Variables: E: strand edges (vein-cell pairs joined by a PIN1 face with P ≥ P_vein); V: vein cells; C: connected components; β_1: closed areole count" ;
    dct:source "Scarpella, Francis & Berleth (2004) Development 131(14):3445-3455 (freely-ending domain fusion); Kang & Dengler (2004) Int. J. Plant Sci. 165(2):231-242 (vein-order hierarchy); standard graph cycle-rank identity" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L815-L860>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L180-L187> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def betti1 (E V C : Int) : Int := E - V + C
theorem vein_graph_growth_event_betti1 (E V C : Int) :
    betti1 (E + 1) (V + 1) C = betti1 E V C ∧
    betti1 E (V + 1) (C + 1) = betti1 E V C ∧
    betti1 (E + 1) V C = betti1 E V C + 1 ∧
    betti1 (E + 1) V (C - 1) = betti1 E V C
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "β_1 = E − V + C;  free-end extension (E+1,V+1,C): Δβ_1 = 0;  new seed (E,V+1,C+1): Δβ_1 = 0;  same-component fusion (E+1,V,C): Δβ_1 = +1;  cross-component fusion (E+1,V,C−1): Δβ_1 = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.betti1" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.vein_graph_growth_event_betti1" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Scarpella et al. (2004) Irreversible Procambial Commitment Lock Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Formalises the irreversible preprocambial → procambial transition that preserves transient bipolar PIN1 cells as permanent bridges, so closed areoles emerge in the committed regime; predicts and the script confirms a monotone non-increasing β_1(τ_commit) (Spearman ρ = −1.0 over τ ∈ {0.5,1,2,4,8}). Code loci: lock #L998-L1001, sweep #L1078-L1103 | Variables: P_ij: membrane PIN1 density on face j of cell i; P_commit: procambial commitment threshold; τ_commit: required sustained-flux duration; locked_ij: irreversible commitment flag (monotone non-decreasing in time)" ;
    dct:source "Scarpella, Francis & Berleth (2004) Development 131(14):3445-3455 (doi 10.1242/dev.01182); Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev. 20(8):1015-1027 (bipolar PIN1 cells)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py#L998-L1001>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean#L201-L217> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def commitment_lock (locked : Bool) (P P_commit : Int) : Int :=
  if locked then (if P < P_commit then P_commit else P) else P
theorem procambial_commitment_lock_monotone (P P_commit : Int) :
    P_commit ≤ commitment_lock true P P_commit ∧
    P ≤ commitment_lock true P P_commit ∧
    (P_commit ≤ P → commitment_lock true P P_commit = P) ∧
    commitment_lock false P P_commit = P
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "timer_ij ← (P_ij ≥ P_commit) ? timer_ij + dt : 0;   locked_ij ← locked_ij ∨ (timer_ij ≥ τ_commit);   P_ij ← locked_ij ? max(P_ij, P_commit) : P_ij" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(65)90077-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1214678>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.commitment_lock" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_035.procambial_commitment_lock_monotone" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

